## Current Progress Stage

The current program progress stage is refinement of the paper carousel
interaction feel on macOS. The latest working-tree changes remove the separate
snap haptic path and make scroll haptics fire only when movement crosses a
paper's main-area threshold. The native macOS handler now responds only to
`paperScroll`, using a two-part `levelChange` then `generic` feedback sequence
to make threshold changes more noticeable.

No persistence, sidebar controls, deletion/reordering, or rich editor behavior
has been added in this stage.

