## Implemented App Behavior

### App Shell

The screen is split into two columns:

- Left sidebar:
  - Fixed width: `260`
  - Dark background: `0xFF20272A`
  - Contains the paper carousel.

- Main workspace:
  - Expanded to fill remaining horizontal space.
  - Light background: `0xFFF1E9DD`
  - Shows an empty prompt until a paper is created.
  - Shows editable selected-paper title and body text after a paper exists.
  - No toolbar, formatting model, rich document canvas, or persistence yet.

### Keyboard Shortcut

`WorkspaceScreen` registers a Flutter `Shortcuts` and `Actions` pair:

- Shortcut: `Meta/Cmd + N`
- Intent: `AddPaperIntent`
- Action: creates a new paper item.

The screen owns a `FocusNode` named `WorkspaceShortcuts`. It requests focus
after the first frame and again when the screen is tapped, so the keyboard
shortcut can remain active.

### Paper Creation

New papers are stored in an in-memory list:

```dart
final List<PaperStackItem> _papers = [];
```

When a paper is created:

- Existing papers are marked unselected.
- A new `PaperStackItem` is appended.
- The new paper receives a generated stable runtime ID:
  - `paper-1`, `paper-2`, `paper-3`, etc.
- The new paper gets a generated title:
  - First paper: `Untitled Paper`
  - Later papers: `Untitled Paper 2`, `Untitled Paper 3`, etc.
- The new paper receives `DateTime.now()` as `createdAt`.
- The new paper starts with empty body content.
- The new paper is marked selected.
- The list is sorted by `createdAt` ascending.

Current limitation: papers are not persisted. Restarting the app loses them.

### Paper Selection

Clicking/tapping a paper preview calls the existing selection path and scrolls
the tapped paper toward the focused carousel position.

Selection still works by:

- Iterating through `_papers`.
- Marking only the tapped paper as selected.
- Using the paper's stable runtime `id` as the identifier.

Current limitation: IDs are stable for the current app run only because there is
no persistence layer yet.

### Main Workspace Editor

The main workspace now contains a basic plain-text editor for the selected
paper.

Behavior:

- If no paper exists, the workspace prompts the user to press Command+N.
- Creating a paper selects it and syncs the title/body editor controllers to
  that paper.
- Typing in the title field renames the selected paper and updates the sidebar
  preview immediately.
- Typing in the editor updates the selected paper's `content` field.
- Switching to another paper syncs the editor to that paper's saved in-memory
  title and content.
- Switching back to a previous paper restores that paper's own content.

The editor is intentionally basic. It uses plain `TextField` controls with no
formatting, blocks, markdown preview, attachments, persistence, undo model, or
file backing.

### Paper Carousel UI

`PaperStack` is a stateful widget exposed with `@visibleForTesting`.

Important constants:

- A4-like height ratio: `1.414`
- Focused paper width factor: `0.70` of available sidebar width
- Viewport height sizing target: paper height capped at `viewport / 3.55`
- Vertical stride factor: `1.03` of paper height
- Focused paper scale: approximately `1.04`
- Neighbour scale: approximately `0.92`
- Farther paper scale floor: `0.82`

Behavior:

- If there are no papers, it renders an empty expanded box.
- Uses `LayoutBuilder` so paper width and height respond to the sidebar size.
- Maintains A4-like paper proportions instead of fixed short card dimensions.
- Uses a smaller paper footprint and viewport-height cap so at least five
  previews can be visible in a standard sidebar view before the user needs to
  scroll more.
- Keeps a small gap between the focused paper and immediate neighbours while
  still leaving farther neighbours partially visible.
- Wraps the stack in a `SingleChildScrollView`.
- Uses `AnimatedBuilder` tied to the scroll controller to recalculate visual
  emphasis while scrolling.
- Calculates a focused index from scroll offset and paper stride.
- Renders only a nearby window of papers around the focused index instead of
  rendering every paper in large collections.
- Sorts layout entries by distance from focus so the focused paper is painted
  above neighbouring papers.
- Calculates paper width, scale, and shadow directly from scroll position so
  scrolling stays responsive and does not restart implicit animations every
  frame.
- Positions papers by their center and scales from `Alignment.center`, so the
  focused paper expands evenly upward and downward.
- Delays selection changes from scroll/tap until after the snap motion, so the
  paper does not suddenly jump bigger before it reaches focus.
- Debounces scroll-end snapping by `140ms` so wheel/trackpad momentum can settle
  before the carousel decides on a resting paper.
- Uses a focus-change threshold of `0.58` paper strides from the currently
  selected paper, so small scroll movements settle back instead of immediately
  selecting the next paper.
- Snaps with a `420ms` ease-out animation.
- Clicking a neighbouring paper selects it and animates it toward focus.
- On macOS, scroll movement triggers strong trackpad haptics only when the
  scroll crosses into another paper's main-area threshold. This is based on the
  rounded paper index from `offset / paperStride`, not continuous movement.
- Scroll haptics use a `90ms` minimum interval to avoid duplicate threshold
  ticks during fast momentum.
- Completed scroll/tap snaps do not trigger haptics.
- Unsupported platforms ignore haptic calls.

There is currently no drag-and-drop behavior in the paper preview code.

### Paper Preview Visuals

`PaperPreview` is a stateless widget exposed with `@visibleForTesting`.

It displays:

- Paper title.
- Short localized creation date.

Visual treatment:

- Paper color: `0xFFFFF7E8`
- Border radius: `7`
- Header top padding: `48`
- Title color: `0xFF28241F`
- Date color: `0xFF756D63`
- Shadow blur and opacity vary based on center focus.
- Selected papers get stronger shadow emphasis.

The current carousel creates a small intentional gap between the enlarged
focused sheet and adjacent papers, while still keeping the physical stack feel.

